A note on the hardware files
----------------------------

The PCB (`kicad/`) and enclosure (`case/`) are covered by the same MIT licence
as the rest of the repository, which is permissive and imposes no
share-alike obligation on derived hardware.

If reciprocal terms are ever wanted for the physical design, the usual choice
for open hardware is **CERN-OHL-S v2**, applied to `kicad/` and `case/` while
leaving firmware and cartridge software under MIT. That change can be made at
any time without affecting anything already released.
